{"tool_name":"forecast","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"FORECasT","home":"https://partslab.sanger.ac.uk/FORECasT","license":"CC-BY-3.0","summary":"Computational predictor of the mutations generated by repair of CRISPR-Cas9-induced double-strand breaks.","addition_date":"2019-06-13T18:46:10Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T21:05:50.449759Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Web application"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:FORECasT","cost":"Free of charge","documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://github.com/felicityallen/SelfTarget/blob/master/README.md"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Nucleic acid sequence","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2977"},"format":[{"term":"Textual format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2330"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Prediction and recognition","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2423"},{"term":"Statistical calculation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2238"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Report","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2048"}}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"FORECasT","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"ELIXIR-EE","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/nbt.4317","metadata":{"abstract":"The DNA mutation produced by cellular repair of a CRISPR\u2013Cas9-generated double-strand break determines its phenotypic effect. It is known that the mutational outcomes are not random, but depend on DNA sequence at the targeted location. Here we systematically study the influence of flanking DNA sequence on repair outcome by measuring the edits generated by >40,000 guide RNAs (gRNAs) in synthetic constructs. We performed the experiments in a range of genetic backgrounds and using alternative CRISPR\u2013Cas9 reagents. In total, we gathered data for >10 9 mutational outcomes. The majority of reproducible mutations are insertions of a single base, short deletions or longer microhomology-mediated deletions. Each gRNA has an individual cell-line-dependent bias toward particular outcomes. We uncover sequence determinants of the mutations produced and use these to derive a predictor of Cas9 editing outcomes. Improved understanding of sequence repair will allow better design of gene editing experiments.","authors":[{"name":"Allen F."},{"name":"Alsinet C."},{"name":"Bassett A.R."},{"name":"Crepaldi L."},{"name":"De Angeli P."},{"name":"Galanty Y."},{"name":"Harding H."},{"name":"Jackson S.P."},{"name":"Khodak A."},{"name":"Kiselev V."},{"name":"Kleshchevnikov V."},{"name":"Kosicki M."},{"name":"Metzakopian E."},{"name":"Munoz-Martinez F."},{"name":"Palenikova P."},{"name":"Parts L."},{"name":"Strong A.J."}],"citationCount":312,"date":"2019-01-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nature Biotechnology","title":"Predicting the mutations generated by repair of Cas9-induced double-strand breaks"},"pmcid":"PMC6949135","pmid":"30480667"}],"topic":[{"term":"Machine learning","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3474"},{"term":"Molecular genetics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3321"},{"term":"Sequence analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0080"},{"term":"Statistics and probability","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2269"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"FORECasT","home":"https://bio.tools/FORECasT","license":"CC-BY-3.0","summary":"Computational predictor of the mutations generated by repair of CRISPR-Cas9-induced double-strand breaks.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:forecast/cmd/partslab.sanger.ac.uk","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":false,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpreted":true,"license":true,"public":true,"readme":true,"repository":{"anonymous":true,"online":true}}},"project":{"build":